# Credentials for the WHO cloud ICD-API, used by the demo's "Servers & auth"
# page. Copy this file to `.env` and fill it in:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored. `.env.example` is not, so never put a real value here.
#
# None of this is needed to start the demo: it boots against WHO's developer
# test server, which takes no credentials. You only need these to exercise the
# cloud API at https://id.who.int, and nothing at all for a local ICD-API
# deployment (Docker, Windows service, systemd) — there you just set the server
# URL in the UI and leave `api_secured` off.

# --- WHO cloud ICD-API (OAUTH 2.0 client credentials) ---------------------- #
# Register at https://icd.who.int/icdapi to get these. They are read by
# `IcdTokenProvider.from_env()`, which runs on the backend: the secret is
# exchanged for a short-lived bearer token and only that token reaches the
# browser, over the Reflex websocket. The secret itself never leaves the
# server, and it is kept out of the provider's `repr()` so it cannot slip into
# a log line or a traceback.
ICD_CLIENT_ID=
ICD_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Optional -------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Only set this if you authenticate against something other than WHO's access
# management service. Defaults to the endpoint below when unset.
# ICD_TOKEN_ENDPOINT=https://icdaccessmanagement.who.int/connect/token

# Never put a bearer token in here. Tokens expire in an hour and the demo
# fetches them on demand from the two variables above; a token pasted into a
# file is a credential sitting on disk with nothing to rotate it.
